# A LIBRARY FILE: definitions only, no `target`, several blocks.
#
# Two jobs, and they are the same fact seen from two sides.
#
# (1) It is what `head_basic.rxt`'s `lib "common.rxt"` RESOLVES TO. W1.1
#     recorded a `lib` path and never looked at it, so `head_basic` could
#     name a file that does not exist and nothing noticed; [DD-13b.W1.2]'s
#     resolver checks the path (existence only — a library's CONTENTS are
#     the composer's, W1.3, and the store scan is [LIB]'s), which is what
#     gives that reference something real to point at.
#
# (2) It is the "a library ships nothing by itself" witness
#     (format_design.md §6.1). No `target`, and MORE THAN ONE block, so
#     the compatibility default (`no target` + exactly one UNNAMED block
#     => `target rx`) does not apply: `pcrec --source` on it builds
#     nothing, at exit 0, which is a DIFFERENT observable from a file it
#     refuses.
description RFC-shaped pieces. Definitions only; this file declares no target.

pattern [a-z]+
name word
m "abc" 0 3
n "123"

pattern [0-9]+
name number
m "42" 0 2
n "xy"
